<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amangkurat II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1703</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amangkurat II was ruler of Mataram from 1677 to 1703, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amangkurat-i">Amangkurat I</a>. To defeat the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trunajaya-rebellion">Trunajaya rebellion</a> he allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>, granting it ports, trade monopolies and payment of its costs. With Company troops he crushed the rebels by 1680 and founded a new capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kartasura">Kartasura</a>, but the alliance left Mataram dependent on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amangkurat-ii.jpg" alt="Amangkurat II" width="320" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tirto (maker, from Gresik) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amangkurat_II_(De_moord_op_kapitein_Tack_in_Kartasura).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
